WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.035
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.937
Another fan favorite,
the log chop.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.405
What I'm gonna do is
take each of your blades

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:09.342
and perform 10 strikes
on this chunk of wood.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.243
This is going to test
the strength of your edge

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.580
and the overall construction
of your knife itself.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.381
Rich, you're up first.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.182
You ready?

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:16.816
 I am.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.218 line:7%
 Let's have some fun.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.987 line:0%
RICH: I intentionally
made my knife heavy,

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.924 line:0%
so it would get through
the chopping test well.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.558
[chopping sounds]

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.094
[rock music]

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:39.472
 About an inch and 3/8 there.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.707
RICH: OK.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.540
 Good job.

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:42.742
 Thank you.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.077
JUDGE: This did very well
cutting into that log.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.647
The one thing, that handle--

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.282
it was very uncomfortable.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.684
It was really putting
pressure on my fingers

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.118
there, trying to hold onto it.

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:54.186
But it cut very well.

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.923
The edge is still razor sharp.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.424
It's nicely done.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.124
 Thank you.

00:00:59.191 --> 00:00:59.959
 Kelly you're up next.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.960
You ready?

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.595
 I'm as ready as I'm gonna get.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.530 line:7%
 Good enough, then.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.338
[chopping sounds]

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.207
[rock music]

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:21.914
JUDGE: Made it down about an
inch and a quarter, Kelly.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:22.915
Nice.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:23.950
Your edge held up great.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.552
It's nice and sharp.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.753
Right now I feel like I'm in
the battle of the giant handles,

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.055
though.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:32.058
It's very rounded, so
those last few strikes,

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.993
I was trying not to have
the blade twist in my hand.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.929
But your edge held
up, so good job.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.198
 Thanks.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:39.999
 What you think, Dave?

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:40.800
You ready?

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.568
 Yep, go for it.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.875
[chopping sounds]

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:53.379
[rock music]

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.519
JUDGE: Went down
an inch and a half.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.520
Good job.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.554
DAVE: Thank you.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.922
JUDGE: Cut very well.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.289
It was actually very
comfortable in the hand.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:06.926
No rollovers, no shiny spots.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.394
Very nice job.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.762
 Thank you.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.765
 Now I'm going to pass you off
to Doug for the sharpness test.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.300
 To test your
blade's sharpness,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.902
I will cut through
the ham three times.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.971
If it's held its edge and is
sharp, it should cut cleanly.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:19.905
Rich, you're up first.

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:20.673
You ready?

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.242
 I am.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.778
[dramatic music playing]

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:37.123
DOUG: Well, Rich, the grip was
a little bit big and blocky.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.525
The weight of the weapon
is a little bit heavy.

00:02:39.591 --> 00:02:42.228
But then again, it cuts
cleanly without even

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.429
having to use power.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.097
It's a very sharp
edge right there.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:46.832
This, sir, will cut.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:47.833
 Thank you.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.701
 Kelly, you're next.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.568
Are you ready?

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:50.270
 Yep.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.237
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:59.412
[dramatic music playing]

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:07.587
Well, Kelly, it glided nicely
and sliced across the meat.

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.623
The issue I have here is a
little bit on your handle.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.324
The area that you
have your bolsters on,

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:14.294
it really digs into my finger.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.030
Overall, though, it's got a nice
feel to it, and it is sharp.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.400
This will cut.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.134
Dave, you're up next.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.002
Are you ready?

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:23.736
 Yes sir.

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:30.210
[dramatic music playing]

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.918
 Well, Dave, the
balance on this blade,

00:03:38.984 --> 00:03:41.020
though, it is light and fast.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.455
And, as you can see,
it lacerates clearly.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:47.860
Your handle
construction is smooth.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.862
It feels good in the hand.

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.031
But your decorated
piece over here?

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.733
If you were a
left-handed practitioner,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.169
it could be a little bit
of an issue for that.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.005
Overall, it will cut.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.006
Good job.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:01.741
 Thank you.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:08.414
HOST: Bladesmiths, your
weapons have been tested,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:12.752
and the judges have
evaluated your work.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:15.655
It's time for one of
you to leave the forge.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:23.496
Kelly, your blade
did not make the cut.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.464 line:0%
JUDGE: Kelly, you did a
great job on your blade,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.934 line:0%
but the real problem
was those bolsters.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.702 line:0%
The bottoms were
so sharp that if I

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.370 line:0%
hadn't been wearing
a glove, it would've

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.439 line:7%
really cut into my hand.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.441
And if a handle's
going to hurt the user,

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.777
then it's not really
a functional weapon.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.413
HOST: Kelly, you have
to surrender your weapon

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.514
and leave the forge.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.253
 To be up against the
clock and to put on a handle

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.591
that I'm happy with is
clearly not my strong suit.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.527
But I got to compete with
some really great guys--

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:57.129
and see that time clock again.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.564
[laughs]

